From: =?utf-8?b?Ik1hcmNvIFRyZXZpc2FuIChUcmV2acOxbyki?= <mail@3v1n0.net>
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2025 12:59:39 +0200
Subject: xdp-app-info: Add separated permissions ID function

While for flatpaks the app-ID matches the value used for permissions
store, in the snap world a snap may contain multiple applications and
they are not fully confined in between each other (processes are, but
they share common data paths), reason why instead of using per-app
permissions we use a per-snap permission.

The snap ID used for permissions is not matching any desktop file or
desktop ID, so this breaks the assumptions of the rest of the stack.

As per this, split the application ID with the permissions ID, by adding
another function that we will re-implement in next commits to have snap
specific behavior.

See: #155 and #769

Origin: https://github.com/flatpak/xdg-desktop-portal/pull/1764
---
 src/xdp-app-info.c | 11 +++++++++++
 src/xdp-app-info.h |  2 ++
 tests/xdp_utils.py |  5 +++++
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/xdp-app-info.c b/src/xdp-app-info.c
index 64624bc..f6109c0 100644
--- a/src/xdp-app-info.c
+++ b/src/xdp-app-info.c
@@ -462,6 +462,17 @@ xdp_app_info_get_id (XdpAppInfo *app_info)
   return priv->id;
 }
 
+const char *
+xdp_app_info_get_permissions_id (XdpAppInfo *app_info)
+{
+  XdpAppInfoPrivate *priv;
+
+  g_return_val_if_fail (app_info != NULL, NULL);
+
+  priv = xdp_app_info_get_instance_private (app_info);
+  return priv->id;
+}
+
 const char *
 xdp_app_info_get_instance (XdpAppInfo *app_info)
 {
